     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" data-account-id=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" accountid=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Andrew Woods</a> <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" data-account-id=\"6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" accountid=\"6089a4c12a753d0071341edb\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Jared Whiklo</a> <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" data-account-id=\"60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" accountid=\"60785e2552404d0070bf1d34\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Danny Bernstein</a></p>\n\n<p>Since storing \"id/jcr:content/fedora:timemap\" isn't an option due to it being a property, these are some options I'm considering for how to store separate timemaps.  I will start with the first option to have something to work with, but I'm open to suggestions:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://gist.github.com/bbpennel/a3682a61fdd030c03a9a3f63fb3dc9fc\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://gist.github.com/bbpennel/a3682a61fdd030c03a9a3f63fb3dc9fc</a></p>",
